{
  "id": "Compound::DB00367 - Gene::5241",
  "verbalization": "Levonorgestrel is implicated in the binding of Pgr through a shared pathway involving progestins. The evidence suggests that Levonorgestrel, through its role in causing genital discharge and premenstrual tension, leads to the activation of Etonogestrel, which in turn binds to Pgr. This indicates a potential mechanism where Levonorgestrel, as a progestin, influences the expression or activity of Pgr via a common intermediate, 3-Oxo-Delta(4) Steroid. The recurring involvement of progestins in this chain highlights a possible dependency on these compounds for Pgr interaction. The integration of these pathways underscores a broader role for progestins in mediating interactions with Pgr, suggesting a functional link between Levonorgestrel and Pgr through a shared biological mechanism.",
